WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.960
Bonnie Wright's 10-year stint as the world's&nbsp;
favorite wizard kid-sister turned her into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:10.960
a plastic-hating, theater-loving mother.&nbsp;
Sometimes growing up can be a magical thing.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.520
Bonnie Wright started casting her spell on&nbsp;
the big screen in 2001's "Harry Potter and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.200
the Sorcerer's Stone," appearing as Ginny&nbsp;
Weasley as her older brothers and Harry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.040
board the Hogwarts Express. She joins them at&nbsp;
Hogwarts a year later in "Harry Potter and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.760
Chamber of Secrets," which finds her being&nbsp;
controlled by Tom Riddle, later revealed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.179
be a younger version of Lord Voldemort.

00:00:32.179 --> 00:00:34.080
Ginny is briefly spotted in "Harry Potter 

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.600
and the Prisoner of Azkaban" and "Harry Potter&nbsp;
and the Goblet of Fire." Her character becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.400
a steady presence as she builds her relationship&nbsp;
with Harry. Wright also noted that her one line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.680
in "Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone"&nbsp;
wasn't added until they went to film the train&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.080
station scene that helps catapult Harry&nbsp;
into his first wizarding adventure. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:57.560
completed scene shows Ginny wishing Harry well,&nbsp;
a suggestion made by director Chris Columbus.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:03.480
"Walk straight to the wall between platforms 9 and&nbsp;
10. Best to do a bit of a run if you're nervous."

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.480
"Good luck."

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:08.600
Wright, like most of the cast, grew up on&nbsp;
the "Harry Potter" set, and as she became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:13.960
a young woman, so did Ginny. In "The Order of the&nbsp;
Phoenix," she joins the group at the Department of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:18.800
Mysteries — where Harry learns about the prophecy&nbsp;
that sets him against Voldemort — and gets to show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:24.440
her tough side by using an impressive "Reducto"&nbsp;
spell against the Death Eaters pursuing them.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:29.120
Wright's role is greatly expanded in "The Half&nbsp;
Blood Prince," getting just as much screen time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.920
as she did in the second film. She now plays&nbsp;
a confident young woman who has friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.720
a boyfriend, and a place in the Slug Club.&nbsp;
Probably her most vital role in the film is her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:43.640
relationship with Daniel Radcliffe's character.&nbsp;
After years of crushing on Harry, the chosen one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:48.840
finally realizes his feelings, and the two begin&nbsp;
to date. She comforts Harry after Dumbledore's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:54.600
death, fights in the Battle of Hogwarts, and&nbsp;
watches her own children head to her alma mater.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.240
After "Harry Potter," Wright appeared in&nbsp;
various independent films, including three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:04.600
in 2013. She played Rose in "The Sea,"&nbsp;
based on the novel by John Banville. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.680
features a man's return to his childhood&nbsp;
beach following the death of his wife.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:12.720
She then played Georgina, an orthopedic&nbsp;
surgeon participating in a "what-if"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.000
scenario to gain entrance to a bunker&nbsp;
in the case of an atomic apocalypse in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.640
the sci-fi psychological thriller "After the&nbsp;
Dark." The film was nominated for Best Motion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:26.744
Picture at The Sitges Film Festival, known&nbsp;
as the world's top fantasy film festival.

00:02:26.744 --> 00:02:31.440
Wright's final role in 2013 was as&nbsp;
Phoebe in "Before I Sleep." The movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.720
which follows a reclusive poet on his search for&nbsp;
peace, premiered at the Heartland Film Festival.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:42.000
In addition to being an actor, Wright has also&nbsp;
tried her hand at directing. In 2012, she made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.040
her directorial debut with the student film,&nbsp;
"Separate We Come, Separate We Go," which follows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:52.000
a 10-year-old girl meeting and becoming friends&nbsp;
with a widowed man Premiering at the Cannes Film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.520
Festival and at the Gold Coast International Film&nbsp;
Festival, the 12-minute film was well-received.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:03.240
She also has directed the short films "Know&nbsp;
Thyself," Fade to Gold," and "Medusa's Ankles."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:08.080
Wright even has some music videos under her&nbsp;
belt, the first of which being "Sea Ess" by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:13.200
George Schuster. She continued directing&nbsp;
music videos in 2018 with "Taught You How&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:18.560
to Feel" by Sophie Lowe, "Iguana Bird' by Pete&nbsp;
Yorn and Scarlett Johansson, and "Fallible" by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:24.520
Maguire. Her next directing project, "Melt,"&nbsp;
was also for Maguire and was released in 2021.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:28.320
Wright is an active spokesperson for&nbsp;
environmentalism, especially when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:32.600
comes to plastic. She has raised awareness&nbsp;
about the dangers of plastic pollution,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:36.440
encouraging fans and friends to&nbsp;
stop relying on single-use plastic.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:41.880
She joined Greenpeace in 2017 to highlight&nbsp;
how single-use plastic has negatively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:45.720
affected our oceans and wildlife and&nbsp;
the importance of beach cleanups.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.680
"I was really saddened to find how much plastic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.480
we found just in that small&nbsp;
hour's worth of trolling."

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:55.120
She participated in the fight against&nbsp;
the Coca-Cola Company — one of the worst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:58.520
producers of plastic pollution,&nbsp;
according to Greenpeace — to stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.680
the production of billions of&nbsp;
plastic bottles. Wright said,

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:05.480
"I'm happy to stand with the&nbsp;
more than 585,000 people who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:09.320
are calling on Coke to phase out its&nbsp;
use of throwaway plastic bottles."

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.800
Wright continues to fight for a cleaner earth&nbsp;
through social media by promoting recycled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:18.160
products, showing the beauty of nature,&nbsp;
and encouraging followers to take action.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:23.960
In April 2022, Wright added author to her&nbsp;
list of job titles, releasing "Go Gently:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.800
Actionable Steps to Nurture&nbsp;
Yourself and the Planet."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:30.800
Wright shares sustainable practices that&nbsp;
readers can regularly practice at home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:34.640
and those tips and tricks have now become&nbsp;
the inspiration for a television series.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.520
Wright shared the news that she&nbsp;
would be creating a new show on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:41.640
the "Go Gently" website in May 2019.&nbsp;
She wrote that production wrapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:46.520
in April 2023. She wrote while sharing&nbsp;
photos of her team surrounded by nature,

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:50.960
"It was such an incredible adventure through&nbsp;
California and Oregon traversing so many different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:56.200
landscapes meeting up with so many incredible&nbsp;
humans doing powerful work to protect our planet."

00:04:56.200 --> 00:05:00.240
As of October 2023, a premiere&nbsp;
date has not been announced. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:03.360
those who can't wait for Wright's&nbsp;
episodic documentary to premiere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.960
she does share ways to practice&nbsp;
sustainability via Instagram and YouTube.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:13.600
In 2013, Wright made her theater debut, sharing&nbsp;
her acting talents in the play "The Moment of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:19.200
Truth," which focuses on a government that is&nbsp;
facing doom as war is on the horizon. The 2013&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:24.960
production marked the first time that the play had&nbsp;
been performed in London since 1951. Wright played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:30.040
the role of The Girl during the show's four-week&nbsp;
summer run at the Southwark Playhouse in London.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:35.320
She told WhatsOnStage that she in no way resembles&nbsp;
her character, which is why she enjoyed playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:39.800
the part. And apparently theater is something that&nbsp;
she has always wanted to explore. She said that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:44.501
she felt like she was trying to navigate an ocean&nbsp;
during the first few days of rehearsals, adding,

00:05:44.501 --> 00:05:50.141
"But I am loving every moment of the challenge,&nbsp;
every day I feel like I am evolving in some way."

00:05:50.141 --> 00:05:54.400
Amid her successful acting career and push&nbsp;
to protect the planet, Wright is growing her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.400 --> 00:06:00.400
family. In April 2023, she and her husband Andrew&nbsp;
Lococo announced that they were expecting their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:05.101
first child by posting a photo of the couple&nbsp;
on Wright's Instagram. She wrote in the post,

00:06:05.101 --> 00:06:09.861
"What a wild and humbling journey pregnancy&nbsp;
is, transforming to make space for new life."

00:06:09.861 --> 00:06:13.040
She has since been chronicling parts&nbsp;
of her pregnancy on the social media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.480
site and posted videos to her YouTube channel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:19.832
discussing nesting and how to keep Earth in&nbsp;
mind when it comes to newborn essentials.

00:06:19.832 --> 00:06:24.080
In an interview with Brides, Wright explained&nbsp;
that she and Lococo met at a New Year's Eve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:30.360
party in 2018 and got engaged in September&nbsp;
2021 with a ring designed by her parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:35.000
Gary Wright and Sheila Teague, who created&nbsp;
the jewelry company Wright &amp; Teague. Wright&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:41.400
and Lococo tied the knot on March 19, 2022, at&nbsp;
a California farm owned by friends. They focused&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:46.280
on using sustainable materials for the wedding&nbsp;
and made a lot of items themselves. She said,

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.320
"We loved the idea of being surrounded by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:52.440
bountiful growing nourishing&nbsp;
plants as we said, 'We do.'"

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:57.360
The wizarding world story has since continued on&nbsp;
stage in the play "Harry Potter and the Cursed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:02.240
Child," which follows the Potter and Weasley&nbsp;
children as they navigate schoolwork and evil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:05.840
leading Harry and his friends to band&nbsp;
together to protect their families.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:11.560
The play first premiered on London's West End&nbsp;
in 2016 and headed to Broadway's Lyric Theatre&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:16.480
in April 2018. Many have wondered if the&nbsp;
play will ever get the big-screen treatment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:21.160
Wright told the "Inside of You with Michael&nbsp;
Rosenbaum" podcast that she is interested in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:25.720
reprising her role in a film adaptation&nbsp;
if the opportunity ever presents itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:29.590
noting that she is currently unaware&nbsp;
of such a project being in the works.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:32.440
"It's not about our characters. So it wouldn't be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:39.760
a massive role ... So it would be fun,&nbsp;
but I have no idea if they'll do it."

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:43.840
Years after the final Harry Potter film,&nbsp;
Wright continues to connect with fans of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:49.920
the franchise. In 2022, she appeared on the&nbsp;
Max TV special "Harry Potter 20th Anniversary:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:54.000
Return to Hogwarts," taking a walk down&nbsp;
memory lane with other cast members.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.640
"To actually get us all in one place was a feat."

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:01.280
She also stopped by the updated Warner Bros.&nbsp;
Studio Tour Hollywood during a pre-opening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:06.760
visit in 2021, exploring the Wizarding World. She&nbsp;
said while walking through the magical attraction,

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:11.640
"I was like, 'We were small, we were tiny,&nbsp;
we were babies!' It was a big revelation."

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:14.600
Wright has also taken to social&nbsp;
media to share her perspective on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:18.840
"Harry Potter" author J.K. Rowling amid&nbsp;
the controversy surrounding Rowling's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:23.200
comments against the transgender&nbsp;
community. In 2020, she wrote on X,

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:27.480
"If 'Harry Potter' was a source of love and&nbsp;
belonging for you, that love is infinite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:32.480
and there to take without judgment or question.&nbsp;
Transwomen are women. I see and love you, Bonnie."

00:08:32.534 --> 00:08:34.614
She told The Times in 2022,

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:37.800
"I made that comment then and I&nbsp;
still stand with that same feeling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:43.040
but it's got to the point where I prefer not to&nbsp;
comment more. It's a subject outside of my input."

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:47.360
While the movies may be over, Bonnie Wright&nbsp;
is still writing this chapter of her career,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:51.000
continuing to work on different Wizarding&nbsp;
World projects. According to the Wizarding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:54.640
World website, Wright is just one of&nbsp;
several big names who lent their voices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:58.520
to the audiobook version of "The Tales&nbsp;
of Beedle the Bard," which is a book made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:03.200
up of five fairy tales. The audiobook&nbsp;
was released on Audible in March 2020.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:08.120
While working on the films, Wright also voiced her&nbsp;
character in the video game adaptations of "Harry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:13.200
Potter and the Order of the Phoenix" and "Harry&nbsp;
Potter and the Half-Blood Prince." She's also been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:17.400
to the "Harry Potter and the Forbidden Journey"&nbsp;
attraction at the Wizarding World of Harry Potter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:23.280
at Universal Studios Florida. In 2014, she took&nbsp;
a tour of the park's Diagon Alley with James&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:28.082
and Oliver Phelps, who played Fred and George&nbsp;
Weasley. The trio were given a look at all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.082 --> 00:09:34.097
the magic that fans can explore in a video posted&nbsp;
to the Universal Orlando Resort YouTube channel.

